Build the library for wasm32-wasip1 (no new behaviour on native targets)

- mimalloc/libmimalloc-sys/notify move to non-wasm target dependencies; the
  library only uses mimalloc in release_import_memory, now a no-op on wasm,
  and notify only in nl-watch.
- term/ptr.rs: wasm32 addresses fit the 48-bit tagged pointers; the
  EnvObj size budget assert is 64-bit only.
- value_checker/tables.rs: fx() is the 64-bit FxHash on 32-bit targets too
  (rustc-hash's FxHasher is usize wide there), so it agrees with fx_at; else
  memo tables rehash entries away from where probe_hashed looks.
- resource.rs: the stack guard reads __stack_low/__stack_high and takes the
  shadow stack pointer from a local's address; on_stack runs inline (no
  threads).
- blake3 for build.rs uses its pure feature: the suite's CC/CFLAGS target wasm.
- memmap2 advice, the threaded read_exact_at import and the signal handlers
  are unix-only.
Upstream: none (no related issues/PRs upstream, checked 2026-11-24).

